---
title: About LearnInsurance
updatedAt: 2026-10-02
---
LearnInsurance explains US insurance words in plain English. It is for people reading their own policy, developers starting on an insurance project, new underwriters, and product owners who need to understand the language quickly.

## What you'll find

- **Terms:** over 1,000 insurance words, each with a short answer, a plain-English definition and an example. Fully written terms also have a diagram, a short real-life story, FAQs and practice questions.
- **Insurance types:** how about 580 kinds of US insurance fit together, from life and health to cyber and crop insurance.
- **Learning paths:** step-by-step paths through the words that matter most, starting with insurance basics.

## How terms are written

Many explanations are written by an AI writer and then checked by a separate AI reviewer against trusted US sources, such as the NAIC, state insurance departments and federal agencies. These pages are marked "AI-generated · AI-reviewed". If something looks wrong, use **Report an issue** on the term page and we'll fix it.

## What we don't do

We explain; we don't advise. We don't sell insurance, recommend products or compare companies. Rules vary by state and by policy, so your own policy wording always decides what is covered.
